##! # Non-Escaping HOF Whitelist
##!
##! Single source of truth for the set of stdlib higher-order-function
##! combinator method names whose closure argument is invoked SYNCHRONOUSLY
##! and NOT stored/spawned. A lambda passed directly as an argument to a call
##! whose (possibly UFCS-canonicalized) method name matches one of these is
##! treated as NON-escaping.
##!
##! Two consumers share this predicate and MUST agree — a divergent escape
##! notion is R-WS4b §6's sharpest one-way-door risk:
##!   - the MIR non-escape analysis (mutable capture-by-ref lowering), and
##!   - the exclusivity (QZ0409) checker's escape oracle.
##! This module is the hoist that retires the former KEEP-IN-SYNC duplicate.
##!
##! Conservative by construction (per the design's load-bearing safety note):
##! a name NOT on this list falls back to by-value / ESCAPING, which is never
##! unsafe.
##!
##! Used by: mir.qz, exclusivity.qz
##! @since 5.12.21

## Returns 1 if `method_name` is on the non-escape whitelist, else 0.
def hof_name_is_nonescaping(method_name: String): Int
  return 1 if method_name.eq("each")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("each_with_index")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("map")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("map_with_index")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("filter")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("reduce")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("fold")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("for_each")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("times")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("any?")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("all?")
  return 1 if method_name.eq("count")
  return 0
end
